<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-export SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/evernote-export4.dtd">
<en-export export-date="20260920T171500Z" application="Evernote" version="10.105.4">
  <note>
    <title>Chicken burrito bowls (meal prep x5)</title>
    <created>20240211T232000Z</created>
    <updated>20251117T000500Z</updated>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Makes 5 bowls. ~45 min total, most of it rice + oven time.</div><div><br/></div><h3>Ingredients</h3><ul><li>2.5 lb boneless skinless chicken thighs</li><li>1.5 cups dry jasmine rice (cooked with 1 tbsp lime juice + cilantro after)</li><li>2 cans black beans, rinsed</li><li>1 bag frozen corn (roast it on the sheet pan with the chicken for the last 10 min)</li><li>1 jar salsa verde</li><li>2 tbsp taco seasoning (or: 2 tsp cumin, 2 tsp chili powder, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1 tsp garlic powder, salt)</li><li>2 limes</li><li>plain nonfat greek yogurt instead of sour cream</li></ul><div><br/></div><h3>Steps</h3><ol><li>Oven 425F. Toss chicken with seasoning + 1 tbsp oil. 22-25 min, internal 175F for thighs.</li><li>Rice cooker: 1.5 cups rice, 2.25 cups water.</li><li>Rest chicken 5 min, chop. Squeeze one lime over it.</li><li>Divide: rice, beans, corn, chicken. Salsa + yogurt go in a separate little container or it gets soggy by day 3.</li></ol><div><br/></div><h3>Macros (per bowl, my numbers from MyFitnessPal)</h3><table style="border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px"><b>kcal</b></td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px"><b>protein</b></td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px"><b>carbs</b></td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px"><b>fat</b></td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px">612</td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px">52 g</td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px">64 g</td><td style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:4px">15 g</td></tr></table><div><br/></div><div>11/16/25: swapped to thighs from breast permanently. way less dry on day 4-5. bumped chicken from 2 lb to 2.5 lb.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Greek yogurt overnight oats</title>
    <created>20240304T034100Z</created>
    <updated>20260119T021200Z</updated>
    <tag>breakfast</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Per jar (make 4 on Sunday night, they last to Thursday):</div><ul><li>1/2 cup rolled oats</li><li>3/4 cup nonfat greek yogurt</li><li>1/2 cup unsweetened almond milk</li><li>1 scoop vanilla whey (~25 g protein)</li><li>1 tbsp chia seeds</li><li>1/2 cup frozen blueberries on top (they thaw overnight)</li><li>pinch of salt + cinnamon</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Shake the whey with the milk first in the jar or it clumps.</div><div><br/></div><div>Macros per jar: ~455 kcal, 44 g protein, 52 g carbs, 8 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>Variations</div><ul><li>PB: swap blueberries for 1 tbsp PB2 + half banana (+60 kcal)</li><li>coffee: 2 oz cold brew instead of half the milk. good before the morning long run</li><li>pumpkin (fall): 1/4 cup canned pumpkin + pumpkin spice</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>1/18/26: wide-mouth pint jars &gt; the plastic tubs, nothing leaks in the backpack.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Turkey chili (big pot)</title>
    <created>20241027T210300Z</created>
    <updated>20251207T214000Z</updated>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>freezer</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Big dutch oven, 7-8 servings. Freezes great in the 32 oz deli containers.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>2 lb 93/7 ground turkey</li><li>1 yellow onion, 1 red bell pepper, 4 cloves garlic</li><li>2 cans kidney beans + 1 can pinto, rinsed</li><li>1 can (28 oz) crushed tomatoes + 1 can diced fire-roasted</li><li>1 cup low sodium chicken broth</li><li>3 tbsp chili powder, 1 tbsp cumin, 2 tsp oregano, 1 tsp cocoa powder (trust it), 1 chipotle in adobo minced</li><li>salt to taste at the end, not the start</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Brown turkey in 2 batches (crowding = gray steamed meat). Onion/pepper 6 min. Spices in for 1 min. Everything else, simmer 45 min lid off the last 15.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving (1/8 pot): 362 kcal, 33 g protein, 34 g carbs, 9 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>Top with greek yogurt + scallions. With 1 cup rice it's ~565 kcal.</div><div><br/></div><div>12/7/25: finals grading week batch. doubled the chipotle, good. froze 4.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Sheet-pan salmon + potatoes</title>
    <created>20250119T235500Z</created>
    <updated>20251026T233000Z</updated>
    <tag>dinner</tag>
    <tag>fish</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>2 servings, 30 min, one pan.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>2 salmon fillets (~6 oz each), skin on</li><li>1 lb baby potatoes halved</li><li>1 bunch asparagus or a bag of green beans</li><li>1 tbsp olive oil, lemon, dill, garlic powder, salt, pepper</li></ul><div><br/></div><ol><li>425F. Potatoes first, oil + salt, 15 min.</li><li>Push potatoes to the edges, salmon in the middle skin down, veg around it. 12 more min.</li><li>Lemon + dill when it comes out.</li></ol><div><br/></div><div>Per serving: 520 kcal, 40 g protein, 38 g carbs, 22 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>Not great as meal prep (reheated salmon smells up the office microwave). Cook it fresh on Mon/Thu.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Egg white muffin cups</title>
    <created>20251110T011400Z</created>
    <updated>20251110T015800Z</updated>
    <tag>breakfast</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>12 cups. Two cups + toast = breakfast during the week.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1 carton (32 oz) liquid egg whites</li><li>4 whole eggs</li><li>1 cup chopped spinach, 1/2 red pepper, 1/2 onion (sauteed first, otherwise watery)</li><li>1/2 cup reduced fat feta</li><li>salt, pepper, everything bagel seasoning on top</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Silicone muffin tray, 350F for 22 min. Let cool in the tray 5 min.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per 2 cups: 168 kcal, 24 g protein, 4 g carbs, 6 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>Note: the metal tray needs a lot of spray, first batch welded itself in. use silicone.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Beef and broccoli (lean)</title>
    <created>20251215T002200Z</created>
    <updated>20251215T011000Z</updated>
    <tag>dinner</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>4 servings.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1.5 lb flank steak, sliced thin against the grain (freeze 20 min first, easier to slice)</li><li>1 big head broccoli (or 2 bags florets)</li><li>Sauce: 1/3 cup low-sodium soy, 2 tbsp oyster sauce, 1 tbsp honey, 1 tbsp cornstarch, 1 tsp sesame oil, 1/2 cup water, garlic + ginger</li><li>1 cup dry rice for 4 portions (cook 2 cups if not cutting)</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Sear beef in 2 batches, very hot pan, 90 s per side. Out. Steam broccoli 3 min in the same pan with a splash of water. Beef back, sauce in, 2 min till glossy.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving (with 1/4 cup dry rice): 478 kcal, 41 g protein, 45 g carbs, 14 g fat.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Protein pancakes</title>
    <created>20260111T150200Z</created>
    <updated>20260111T154000Z</updated>
    <tag>breakfast</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Sunday after long run. Makes ~8 small pancakes, 2 servings.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1 cup oat flour (blend rolled oats)</li><li>1 scoop vanilla whey</li><li>1 tsp baking powder, pinch salt, cinnamon</li><li>2 eggs</li><li>3/4 cup nonfat greek yogurt</li><li>1/3 cup milk (more if thick)</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Medium-low heat, they burn fast because of the whey. Flip when edges look dry.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving: 405 kcal, 37 g protein, 42 g carbs, 9 g fat (before syrup; 2 tbsp real maple = +104 kcal).</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Lentil dal + rice</title>
    <created>20260222T234400Z</created>
    <updated>20260223T005100Z</updated>
    <tag>dinner</tag>
    <tag>vegetarian</tag>
    <tag>cheap</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Cheap week recipe. 6 servings.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>2 cups red lentils, rinsed until water runs mostly clear</li><li>1 onion, 4 garlic, thumb of ginger</li><li>1 can diced tomatoes, 1 can light coconut milk, 4 cups water</li><li>2 tsp turmeric, 2 tsp cumin, 1 tsp garam masala, 1/2 tsp chili flakes</li><li>spinach at the end, lemon</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Onion 8 min, garlic/ginger/spices 1 min, lentils + tomatoes + water 25 min stirring. Coconut milk last 5 min.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving dal only: 318 kcal, 18 g protein, 46 g carbs, 7 g fat. Low protein by my standards -&gt; serve with 2 eggs or a chicken thigh on the side.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Meal prep Sunday — shopping list template</title>
    <created>20260125T163000Z</created>
    <updated>20260308T160500Z</updated>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>shopping</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Copy this every Sunday. Kroger on Prices Fork, go before 10.</div><div><br/></div><h3>Protein</h3><div><en-todo checked="false"/>chicken thighs 2.5 lb</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>93/7 ground turkey 2 lb (every other week)</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>eggs 18</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>egg whites carton</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>nonfat greek yogurt 32 oz x2</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>cottage cheese 24 oz</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>whey (check tub, ~6 scoops left = buy)</div><h3>Carbs</h3><div><en-todo checked="false"/>jasmine rice (bulk)</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>rolled oats</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>potatoes 3 lb</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>bananas x7</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>frozen blueberries</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>tortillas (high fiber)</div><h3>Veg</h3><div><en-todo checked="false"/>spinach, broccoli, bell peppers x3, onions, garlic</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>frozen corn + green beans</div><h3>Other</h3><div><en-todo checked="false"/>salsa verde, soy sauce, chipotle in adobo</div><div><en-todo checked="false"/>coffee</div><div><br/></div><div>Budget target: under $95/week. Last 4 weeks: $88, $102 (whey), $79, $91.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Cottage cheese pasta sauce</title>
    <created>20260316T004000Z</created>
    <updated>20260316T010200Z</updated>
    <tag>dinner</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Saw this everywhere, actually good.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1 cup low-fat cottage cheese</li><li>1/2 cup jarred marinara</li><li>1/4 cup parmesan</li><li>garlic, chili flakes, basil</li></ul><div>Blend until smooth, warm gently in a pan (don't boil, it splits).</div><div><br/></div><div>Over 3 oz dry protein pasta (Barilla Protein+) + 4 oz chicken breast:</div><div>~720 kcal, 74 g protein, 76 g carbs, 13 g fat. Big bowl.</div><div><br/></div><div>Next time: add roasted red peppers to the blender.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Post-long-run smoothie</title>
    <created>20260510T151800Z</created>
    <updated>20260510T152500Z</updated>
    <tag>smoothie</tag>
    <tag>recovery</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Within 30 min of anything over 90'.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1 banana (frozen)</li><li>1 cup frozen mango</li><li>1 scoop whey</li><li>1 cup skim milk</li><li>1 tbsp honey</li><li>pinch of salt (actually helps on hot days)</li><li>ice</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>~520 kcal, 36 g protein, 88 g carbs, 3 g fat. Roughly 3:1 carb:protein which is what the coach article said.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Chicken shawarma wraps</title>
    <created>20260614T221000Z</created>
    <updated>20260614T233500Z</updated>
    <tag>dinner</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Marinade the night before. 6 wraps.</div><div><br/></div><div>Marinade (for 2 lb thighs): 1/2 cup nonfat greek yogurt, juice of 1 lemon, 3 garlic, 2 tsp cumin, 2 tsp paprika, 1 tsp coriander, 1/2 tsp turmeric, 1/2 tsp cinnamon, salt.</div><div><br/></div><div>Bake 425F 25 min on a rack, then broil 3 min for the char. Slice.</div><div><br/></div><div>Wrap: high-fiber tortilla, chicken, cucumber/tomato/red onion, garlic yogurt sauce (yogurt + garlic + lemon + dill).</div><div><br/></div><div>Per wrap: 445 kcal, 41 g protein, 30 g carbs, 16 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>Rebuttal week dinner. made these 2x.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Overnight chia pudding</title>
    <created>20260824T044000Z</created>
    <updated>20260824T045800Z</updated>
    <tag>breakfast</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>For the SF fridge (shared kitchen, label the jar!). 4 servings.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1/2 cup chia seeds</li><li>2 cups unsweetened soy milk</li><li>1 cup nonfat greek yogurt</li><li>2 scoops vanilla protein</li><li>2 tbsp maple</li><li>vanilla, pinch salt</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Whisk, rest 10 min, whisk again (prevents clumps), fridge overnight. Top with berries.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving: 330 kcal, 27 g protein, 26 g carbs, 13 g fat.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
